1. Dependencies
---------------

Requires libglib2.0-dev, ctags, openssl, cmake, libwebsockets4.3.3, npm, libjson-c-dev

on debian 12-

`apt-get install gcc libglib2.0-dev exuberant-ctags openssl cmake npm libjson-c-dev libsqlite3-dev pkg-config libzstd-dev`

1.a Libwebsockets
-----------------

Libwesockets in debian 11 is the wrong version, and in debian 12
doesn't have the required options compiled in.  So, you've got to get the code
from https://libwebsockets.org/repo/libwebsockets and rebuild it.

Note that for the cmake step....
# -DLWS_IPV6=ON because in deb 11 at least, that wasn't the default.
	(But, it looks like IPV6 may be the lws default going forward, after commit
	0fed1e15afe745989f929194c31bb8fb46fa37a8 to lws main)
# -DLWS_WITHOUT_EXTENSIONS=0 enables permessage deflate, and IS REQUIRED by LociTerm
# -DLWS_WITH_LIBUV=ON to enable libuv loop timers, and IS REQUIRED by LociTerm
# -DLWS_WITH_EVENT_LIBS=ON to enable event libraries, and IS REQUIRED by LociTerm
### -DLWS_WITH_SYS_ASYNC_DNS=1 because the default is 0, and the scanner needs async
	( Not recommended in v4.4-stable or v4.5-stable, due to lws bugs, HOWEVER
	after 
	commit f06bf536c9de123e9ffa99ff8ac2d03ad0717ad2 (HEAD -> main, origin/main, origin/HEAD) 
	Author: Andy Green <andy@warmcat.com> 
	Date:   Sun Jan 25 20:24:54 2026 +0000 
	it looks like the ASYNC_DNS problems may have been fixed!)
### -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=DEBUG will make a debug image of libwebsockets. Not normally used.

cd ~/othercode
git clone --branch v4.4-stable https://libwebsockets.org/repo/libwebsockets
cd libwebsockets
mkdir build
cd build
cmake -DLWS_IPV6=ON -DLWS_WITH_ZLIB=ON -DLWS_WITHOUT_EXTENSIONS=OFF -DLWS_WITH_LIBUV=ON -DLWS_WITH_EVENT_LIBS=ON -DLWS_WITH_SYS_ASYNC_DNS=0 ..
make
sudo make install

